{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_0121Ann4YGftXFYvEDmi6KLD","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t# 2026-04-13-2100-prealloc-gkr-input-buffers\n2\t\n3\tPre-allocate per-thread reusable GPU buffers for GKR input evaluation to eliminate per-AIR memory management overhead and unlock multi-stream concurrency. Currently, each of the ~310 per-segment AIRs allocates and frees an `intermediates` DeviceBuffer through the global `Mutex<MemoryManager>`, which also calls `cudaMallocAsync`/`cudaFreeAsync` on the per-thread CUDA stream pool. This serializes the 8 worker threads via both the Rust mutex and implicit CUDA pool synchronization, producing ~1.0x effective parallelism (529ms wall for 471ms GPU kernel time). Pre-allocating max-sized buffers per thread before spawning workers should eliminate ~2500 lock acquisitions per segment and all per-AIR CUDA pool operations, enabling real kernel concurrency and targeting a 1.5–2.5x reduction in GKR input eval wall time.\n4\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"8112afd3-6b71-4b0c-b23a-9001717999d3","uuid":"3975bc3e-ad1f-40dd-8f26-6384b5761002","timestamp":"2026-04-13T04:24:36.562Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/home/georg/stark-backend/autoopt-results/task.md","content":"# 2026-04-13-2100-prealloc-gkr-input-buffers\n\nPre-allocate per-thread reusable GPU buffers for GKR input evaluation to eliminate per-AIR memory management overhead and unlock multi-stream concurrency. Currently, each of the ~310 per-segment AIRs allocates and frees an `intermediates` DeviceBuffer through the global `Mutex<MemoryManager>`, which also calls `cudaMallocAsync`/`cudaFreeAsync` on the per-thread CUDA stream pool. This serializes the 8 worker threads via both the Rust mutex and implicit CUDA pool synchronization, producing ~1.0x effective parallelism (529ms wall for 471ms GPU kernel time). Pre-allocating max-sized buffers per thread before spawning workers should eliminate ~2500 lock acquisitions per segment and all per-AIR CUDA pool operations, enabling real kernel concurrency and targeting a 1.5–2.5x reduction in GKR input eval wall time.\n","numLines":4,"startLine":1,"totalLines":4}}}
