{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_015PUCKa8WA3Dv4WSUmvRnC2","type":"tool_result","content":"commit b406a5551020e9c5e0a119790fc7056c7d76636f\nAuthor: Claude <claude@anthropic.com>\nDate:   Mon Apr 13 00:09:37 2026 +0200\n\n    Batch stacked reduction MLE sync: eliminate per-window GPU pipeline drains\n    \n    Replace per-window D2H synchronization in batch_sumcheck_poly_eval() with\n    a single fill_zero + to_host per MLE round. Both CUDA kernels already use\n    atomic accumulation into d_accum, so per-window syncs were unnecessary.\n    \n    Changes:\n    - Accept raw *const EF in degenerate kernel wrapper (pointer offset into\n      bulk-uploaded eq_ub buffer)\n    - Allocate d_eq_ub_all for full unstacked_cols instead of per-window d_eq_ub\n    - Upload eq_ub_per_trace once per round, fill_zero once, to_host once\n    - Remove per-window reallocation and collection/sum of s_evals_batch\n    \n    At APC 300: Stacked Reduction MLE rounds 280ms -> 95ms (2.95x),\n    Stacked Reduction total 312ms -> 126ms (2.48x),\n    STARK excl trace 2460ms -> 2268ms (1.08x lower).\n    \n    Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.6 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n crates/cuda-backend/src/cuda/stacked_reduction.rs |  4 +-\n crates/cuda-backend/src/stacked_reduction.rs      | 58 ++++++++---------------\n 2 files changed, 22 insertions(+), 40 deletions(-)","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_01SsLpYZqsjSNJyvURFPPJ4p","session_id":"8112afd3-6b71-4b0c-b23a-9001717999d3","uuid":"af3da256-5711-4f4e-acc0-6547d1e53ef6","timestamp":"2026-04-13T04:31:27.597Z"}
