{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_013QDcsGGRHfCLgppvAmnV66","type":"tool_result","content":"//! buffers are freed via cudaFreeAsync through the VPMM pool, so frees are only stream-ordered. If\n//! new allocations happen before the current stream is synchronized, physical peak memory can\n//! max. Callers that care about physical peak should ensure a current-stream sync after use (e.g.\n//! by calling `to_host()` on outputs or `current_stream_sync()`).\n    stream::current_stream_sync,\n/// Number of OS threads (and thus CUDA streams) for parallel Round 0 processing.\n        let q_evals = sum_buffer.to_host_on_current_stream()?;\n        let evals = sum.to_host_on_current_stream()?;\n        // is visible to worker thread streams.\n        current_stream_sync().map_err(MemCopyError::from)?;","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_01VJiYRQA9nt5XbKFFAXpUpv","session_id":"8112afd3-6b71-4b0c-b23a-9001717999d3","uuid":"3d8fa6ca-4cb6-43c5-bd7d-198525c626c9","timestamp":"2026-04-13T04:31:33.404Z"}
