{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-6","id":"msg_01LzjMxstvDjQ2w6xmD8HbRz","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01JhhpL9odmyDM1MFyNYaifQ","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/home/georg/stark-backend/autoopt-results/task.md","content":"# 2026-04-13-2300-batch-mle-round-kernels\n\nReplace the per-AIR kernel launch loop in `batch_sumcheck_poly_eval` (stacked reduction MLE rounds) with batched kernel launches using descriptor arrays. Currently, each MLE round iterates over ~600 AIR windows and launches one kernel per window (10K+ degenerate + 5K+ non-degenerate launches per benchmark), but total GPU compute is only 62ms while wall time is 182ms at APC 300. Batching all per-AIR launches into 1-2 kernel launches per round (using the proven descriptor array pattern from the stacking scatter kernel) will eliminate ~15K kernel launches, improve GPU SM utilization through concurrent block execution, and reduce CPU loop overhead — targeting a 50-100ms reduction in MLE Rounds time at APC 300.\n"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":3082,"cache_read_input_tokens":104146,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":3082},"output_tokens":8,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"8112afd3-6b71-4b0c-b23a-9001717999d3","uuid":"2eaa6bf7-df31-4c8b-8f1e-fc6982dca86f"}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01JhhpL9odmyDM1MFyNYaifQ","type":"tool_result","content":"The file /home/georg/stark-backend/autoopt-results/task.md has been updated successfully."}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"8112afd3-6b71-4b0c-b23a-9001717999d3","uuid":"a2f9c71d-7961-4bd0-ad93-b5b922df39b2","timestamp":"2026-04-13T04:37:33.508Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"update","filePath":"/home/georg/stark-backend/autoopt-results/task.md","content":"# 2026-04-13-2300-batch-mle-round-kernels\n\nReplace the per-AIR kernel launch loop in `batch_sumcheck_poly_eval` (stacked reduction MLE rounds) with batched kernel launches using descriptor arrays. Currently, each MLE round iterates over ~600 AIR windows and launches one kernel per window (10K+ degenerate + 5K+ non-degenerate launches per benchmark), but total GPU compute is only 62ms while wall time is 182ms at APC 300. Batching all per-AIR launches into 1-2 kernel launches per round (using the proven descriptor array pattern from the stacking scatter kernel) will eliminate ~15K kernel launches, improve GPU SM utilization through concurrent block execution, and reduce CPU loop overhead — targeting a 50-100ms reduction in MLE Rounds time at APC 300.\n","structuredPatch":[{"oldStart":1,"oldLines":3,"newStart":1,"newLines":3,"lines":["-# 2026-04-13-2100-prealloc-gkr-input-buffers","+# 2026-04-13-2300-batch-mle-round-kernels"," ","-Pre-allocate per-thread reusable GPU buffers for GKR input evaluation to eliminate per-AIR memory management overhead and unlock multi-stream concurrency. Currently, each of the ~310 per-segment AIRs allocates and frees an `intermediates` DeviceBuffer through the global `Mutex<MemoryManager>`, which also calls `cudaMallocAsync`/`cudaFreeAsync` on the per-thread CUDA stream pool. This serializes the 8 worker threads via both the Rust mutex and implicit CUDA pool synchronization, producing ~1.0x effective parallelism (529ms wall for 471ms GPU kernel time). Pre-allocating max-sized buffers per thread before spawning workers should eliminate ~2500 lock acquisitions per segment and all per-AIR CUDA pool operations, enabling real kernel concurrency and targeting a 1.5–2.5x reduction in GKR input eval wall time.","+Replace the per-AIR kernel launch loop in `batch_sumcheck_poly_eval` (stacked reduction MLE rounds) with batched kernel launches using descriptor arrays. Currently, each MLE round iterates over ~600 AIR windows and launches one kernel per window (10K+ degenerate + 5K+ non-degenerate launches per benchmark), but total GPU compute is only 62ms while wall time is 182ms at APC 300. Batching all per-AIR launches into 1-2 kernel launches per round (using the proven descriptor array pattern from the stacking scatter kernel) will eliminate ~15K kernel launches, improve GPU SM utilization through concurrent block execution, and reduce CPU loop overhead — targeting a 50-100ms reduction in MLE Rounds time at APC 300."]}],"originalFile":"# 2026-04-13-2100-prealloc-gkr-input-buffers\n\nPre-allocate per-thread reusable GPU buffers for GKR input evaluation to eliminate per-AIR memory management overhead and unlock multi-stream concurrency. Currently, each of the ~310 per-segment AIRs allocates and frees an `intermediates` DeviceBuffer through the global `Mutex<MemoryManager>`, which also calls `cudaMallocAsync`/`cudaFreeAsync` on the per-thread CUDA stream pool. This serializes the 8 worker threads via both the Rust mutex and implicit CUDA pool synchronization, producing ~1.0x effective parallelism (529ms wall for 471ms GPU kernel time). Pre-allocating max-sized buffers per thread before spawning workers should eliminate ~2500 lock acquisitions per segment and all per-AIR CUDA pool operations, enabling real kernel concurrency and targeting a 1.5–2.5x reduction in GKR input eval wall time.\n"}}
