{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_013Rxf9y1FMAncXUpJpB71s3","type":"tool_result","content":"28-/// Defines FpExt, a finite field F_p^4, based on Fp via the irreducible polynomial x^4 - 11.\n29-\n30-#include \"fp.h\"\n31-\n32-/// Instances of FpExt are element of a finite field F_p^4.  They are represented as elements of\n33-/// F_p[X] / (X^4 - 11). Basically, this is a 'big' finite field (about 2^128 elements), which is\n34-/// used when the security of various operations depends on the size of the field.  It has the field\n35-/// Fp as a subfield, which means operations by the two are compatible, which is important.  The\n36-/// irreducible polynomial was chosen to be the simplest possible one, x^4 - B, where 11 is the\n37-/// smallest B which makes the polynomial irreducible.\n38:struct FpExt {\n39-    /// The elements of FpExt, elems[0] + elems[1]*X + elems[2]*X^2 + elems[3]*x^4\n40-    union {\n41-        Fp elems[4];\n42-        bb31_4_t rep;\n43-    };\n44-    \n45-    /// Default constructor makes the zero elements\n46-    __device__ FpExt() : rep(bb31_t{0u}) {}\n47-\n48-    /// Initialize from uint32_t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_01UoZbyyAskFa8pFfdV2Rnqz","session_id":"8112afd3-6b71-4b0c-b23a-9001717999d3","uuid":"8507b605-a998-4f8f-85f4-9294ce38a030","timestamp":"2026-04-13T04:40:46.566Z"}
