{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_0148bJ3HEMPN4bNL9YKiPzNv","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t# Plan: Batch MLE Round Kernels\n2\t\n3\t## Goal\n4\t\n5\tReplace the per-AIR kernel launch loop in `batch_sumcheck_poly_eval()` with batched kernel launches using descriptor arrays. This eliminates ~15K individual kernel launches per benchmark at APC 300, improving GPU utilization and reducing host-side overhead.\n6\t\n7\t**Target**: Reduce MLE Rounds from 182ms to ~80-130ms at APC 300 (save 50-100ms). No regression at APC 0.\n8\t\n9\t## Current Code Path\n10\t\n11\t### Rust entry point\n12\t`crates/cuda-backend/src/stacked_reduction.rs:789` — `batch_sumcheck_poly_eval()`\n13\t\n14\tPer MLE round (rounds 1..=n_stack):\n15\t1. **Line 831**: `fill_zero(d_accum)` — zeros the 8-element u64 atomic accumulator\n16\t2. **Line 828**: `eq_ub_per_trace.copy_to(d_eq_ub_all)` — bulk H2D upload (once per round)\n17\t3. **Lines 835-888**: Loop over `ht_diff_idxs.windows(2)`:\n18\t   - Compute per-window pointers: `unstacked_cols_ptr = d_unstacked_cols.as_ptr().add(window[0])`, `lambda_pows_ptr = d_lambda_pows.as_ptr().add(2 * window[0])`\n19\t   - **Line 845**: Branch on `log_height < l_skip + round` → degenerate vs non-degenerate\n20\t   - **Degenerate (line 852)**: `stacked_reduction_sumcheck_mle_round_degenerate()` — 1 block, min(window_len, 256) threads\n21\t   - **Non-degenerate (line 873)**: `stacked_reduction_sumcheck_mle_round()` — grid.x × grid.y blocks with auto-tuned stride\n22\t4. **Line 891**: `d_accum.to_host()` — single D2H copy + CPU reduction\n23\t\n24\t### CUDA kernels\n25\t`crates/cuda-backend/cuda/src/stacked_reduction.cu`\n26\t\n27\t**Degenerate kernel** (line 306): Single block per AIR. Each thread iterates over window columns at stride=blockDim.x. Loads per-column q_eval from global memory, multiplies by eq/lambda factors, accumulates via `block_reduce_sum` + `atomic_add_fpext_to_u64` to shared output.\n28\t\n29\t**Non-degenerate kernel** (line 228): 2D grid (y_dim blocks × window_stride blocks). Each thread handles one y-point, iterates over window columns at stride=gridDim.y. Same atomic accumulation to shared output.\n30\t\n31\tBoth kernels accumulate into the SAME `d_accum` buffer via atomics → all per-AIR launches within a round are data-independent and can execute concurrently.\n32\t\n33\t### FFI bindings\n34\t`crates/cuda-backend/src/cuda/stacked_reduction.rs`\n35\t- Lines 53-64: `_stacked_reduction_sumcheck_mle_round` extern declaration\n36\t- Lines 66-78: `_stacked_reduction_sumcheck_mle_round_degenerate` extern declaration\n37\t- Lines 209-231: Safe wrapper `stacked_reduction_sumcheck_mle_round()`\n38\t- Lines 245-275: Safe wrapper `stacked_reduction_sumcheck_mle_round_degenerate()`\n39\t\n40\t### Why it's slow\n41\t\n42\tAt APC 300 with 2 segments (~311 AIRs/segment, ~17 MLE rounds):\n43\t- **10,348 degenerate kernel launches**: avg 3.9μs each, 40ms total GPU time\n44\t- **5,076 non-degenerate kernel launches**: avg 4.3μs each, 22ms total GPU time\n45\t- **Total**: 15,424 launches, 62ms GPU time, **182ms wall time**\n46\t- **120ms overhead** (66%) from: kernel launch latency (~30ms), GPU pipeline gaps between tiny launches (~40ms), CPU loop overhead (~20ms), sequential execution on single stream preventing SM utilization (~30ms)\n47\t\n48\tEach degenerate launch uses 1 block on 1 SM. The RTX 4090 has 128 SMs. Effective utilization: ~0.8% per launch.\n49\t\n50\t## Changes\n51\t\n52\t### Change 1: Add descriptor structs (CUDA side)\n53\t\n54\t**File**: `crates/cuda-backend/cuda/src/stacked_reduction.cu`\n55\t\n56\tAdd two new structs after the existing `UnstackedSlice` (line 34):\n57\t\n58\t```c\n59\tstruct DegenMleDesc {\n60\t    uint32_t col_offset;    // = window[0], indexes into unstacked_cols, eq_ub, lambda_pows\n61\t    uint32_t window_len;    // = window[1] - window[0]\n62\t    FpExt eq_r;             // from eq_stable[log_height]\n63\t    FpExt k_rot_r;          // from k_rot_stable[log_height]\n64\t};\n65\t\n66\tstruct NonDegenMleDesc {\n67\t    uint32_t col_offset;    // = window[0]\n68\t    uint32_t window_len;    // = window[1] - window[0]\n69\t    uint32_t num_y;         // = 1 << (log_height - l_skip - round)\n70\t    uint32_t stride;        // auto-tuned grid.y from existing heuristic\n71\t    uint32_t blocks_x;      // = ceil(num_y / 256)\n72\t};\n73\t```\n74\t\n75\t### Change 2: Add batched degenerate kernel (CUDA side)\n76\t\n77\t**File**: `crates/cuda-backend/cuda/src/stacked_reduction.cu`\n78\t\n79\tAdd new kernel after the existing degenerate kernel (after line 368):\n80\t\n81\t```cuda\n82\t__global__ void batched_degenerate_mle_round_kernel(\n83\t    const DegenMleDesc *__restrict__ descs,\n84\t    const FpExt *__restrict__ const *__restrict__ q_evals,\n85\t    const FpExt *__restrict__ eq_ub_base,\n86\t    const UnstackedSlice *__restrict__ unstacked_cols_base,\n87\t    const FpExt *__restrict__ lambda_pows_base,\n88\t    uint64_t *__restrict__ output,\n89\t    uint32_t q_height,\n90\t    uint32_t shift_factor)\n91\t```\n92\t\n93\t**Grid**: `(num_degenerate_airs, 1)`, **Block**: `(256, 1)`\n94\t\n95\tEach block reads `descs[blockIdx.x]` to get its col_offset, window_len, eq_r, k_rot_r. Computes base pointers: `eq_ub_ptr = eq_ub_base + desc.col_offset`, `unstacked_cols = unstacked_cols_base + desc.col_offset`, `lambda_pows = lambda_pows_base + 2 * desc.col_offset`. Body is identical to existing degenerate kernel (lines 328-358) but using descriptor fields instead of kernel args. Threads with `threadIdx.x >= desc.window_len` contribute zero to the reduction (handled naturally by the for-loop bounds).\n96\t\n97\t### Change 3: Add batched non-degenerate kernel (CUDA side)\n98\t\n99\t**File**: `crates/cuda-backend/cuda/src/stacked_reduction.cu`\n100\t\n101\tAdd new kernel after the batched degenerate kernel:\n102\t\n103\t```cuda\n104\t__global__ void batched_nondegen_mle_round_kernel(\n105\t    const NonDegenMleDesc *__restrict__ descs,\n106\t    const uint32_t *__restrict__ block_prefix_sums,\n107\t    uint32_t num_descs,\n108\t    const FpExt *__restrict__ const *__restrict__ q_evals,\n109\t    const FpExt *__restrict__ eq_r_ns,\n110\t    const FpExt *__restrict__ k_rot_ns,\n111\t    const UnstackedSlice *__restrict__ unstacked_cols_base,\n112\t    const FpExt *__restrict__ lambda_pows_base,\n113\t    uint64_t *__restrict__ output,\n114\t    uint32_t q_height)\n115\t```\n116\t\n117\t**Grid**: `(total_blocks, 1)` where `total_blocks = sum of (blocks_x * stride) for all non-degenerate AIRs`, **Block**: `(256, 1)`\n118\t\n119\tEach block uses binary search on `block_prefix_sums` to find its AIR index (`air_idx`), then computes its local block index within that AIR. Decomposes local index into `(local_x, local_y) = (local_block % blocks_x, local_block / blocks_x)`. Maps to `y_int = local_x * 256 + threadIdx.x` and `window_idx_base = local_y`. Rest of computation is identical to existing non-degenerate kernel (lines 254-291).\n120\t\n121\tBinary search is O(log N) per block — at most ~10 comparisons for 600 AIRs. Negligible overhead.\n122\t\n123\t### Change 4: Add launcher functions (CUDA side)\n124\t\n125\t**File**: `crates/cuda-backend/cuda/src/stacked_reduction.cu`\n126\t\n127\tAdd two new extern \"C\" launcher functions after the existing launchers (after line 570):\n128\t\n129\t`_batched_stacked_reduction_sumcheck_mle_round_degenerate`:\n130\t- Receives: descs ptr, num_descs, shared array pointers, q_height, shift_factor\n131\t- Grid: `(num_descs, 1)`, Block: `(256, 1)`\n132\t- shmem: `div_ceil(256, WARP_SIZE) * sizeof(FpExt) = 8 * 16 = 128 bytes`\n133\t\n134\t`_batched_stacked_reduction_sumcheck_mle_round`:\n135\t- Receives: descs ptr, block_prefix_sums ptr, num_descs, total_blocks, shared array pointers, q_height\n136\t- Grid: `(total_blocks, 1)`, Block: `(256, 1)`\n137\t- shmem: same 128 bytes\n138\t- Computes auto-tuned stride per descriptor using existing heuristic (lines 505-524), populates stride and blocks_x fields on the host side (Rust) before upload.\n139\t\n140\t### Change 5: Add Rust descriptor types and FFI bindings\n141\t\n142\t**File**: `crates/cuda-backend/src/cuda/stacked_reduction.rs`\n143\t\n144\tAdd `#[repr(C)]` Rust structs matching the CUDA descriptors:\n145\t\n146\t```rust\n147\t#[repr(C)]\n148\t#[derive(Clone, Copy)]\n149\tpub(crate) struct DegenMleDesc {\n150\t    col_offset: u32,\n151\t    window_len: u32,\n152\t    eq_r: EF,\n153\t    k_rot_r: EF,\n154\t}\n155\t\n156\t#[repr(C)]\n157\t#[derive(Clone, Copy)]\n158\tpub(crate) struct NonDegenMleDesc {\n159\t    col_offset: u32,\n160\t    window_len: u32,\n161\t    num_y: u32,\n162\t    stride: u32,\n163\t    blocks_x: u32,\n164\t}\n165\t```\n166\t\n167\tAdd extern declarations for the new launcher functions. Add safe Rust wrappers that take `&DeviceBuffer<DegenMleDesc>` / `&DeviceBuffer<NonDegenMleDesc>` and the shared base pointers.\n168\t\n169\t### Change 6: Modify batch_sumcheck_poly_eval to use batched launches\n170\t\n171\t**File**: `crates/cuda-backend/src/stacked_reduction.rs`\n172\t\n173\tReplace the per-window loop (lines 835-888) with:\n174\t\n175\t**Phase A — Build descriptors** (CPU-only, no CUDA calls):\n176\t```rust\n177\tlet mut degen_descs: Vec<DegenMleDesc> = Vec::new();\n178\tlet mut nondegen_descs: Vec<NonDegenMleDesc> = Vec::new();\n179\tlet mut nondegen_block_offsets: Vec<u32> = Vec::new();\n180\tlet mut total_nondegen_blocks: u32 = 0;\n181\t\n182\tfor window in self.ht_diff_idxs.windows(2) {\n183\t    let col_offset = window[0] as u32;\n184\t    let window_len = (window[1] - window[0]) as u32;\n185\t    let log_height = self.unstacked_cols[window[0]].log_height as usize;\n186\t\n187\t    if log_height < l_skip + round {\n188\t        degen_descs.push(DegenMleDesc {\n189\t            col_offset,\n190\t            window_len,\n191\t            eq_r: self.eq_stable[log_height],\n192\t            k_rot_r: self.k_rot_stable[log_height],\n193\t        });\n194\t    } else {\n195\t        let hypercube_dim = log_height - l_skip - round;\n196\t        let num_y = 1u32 << hypercube_dim;\n197\t        let (blocks_x, stride) = compute_mle_launch_params(num_y, window_len, self.sm_count);\n198\t        nondegen_block_offsets.push(total_nondegen_blocks);\n199\t        total_nondegen_blocks += blocks_x * stride;\n200\t        nondegen_descs.push(NonDegenMleDesc {\n201\t            col_offset, window_len, num_y, stride, blocks_x,\n202\t        });\n203\t    }\n204\t}\n205\t```\n206\t\n207\t**Phase B — Upload descriptors and launch batched kernels**:\n208\t```rust\n209\tif !degen_descs.is_empty() {\n210\t    let d_degen_descs = degen_descs.to_device()?;\n211\t    batched_stacked_reduction_sumcheck_mle_round_degenerate(\n212\t        &d_degen_descs,\n213\t        &self.d_q_eval_ptrs,\n214\t        self.d_eq_ub_all.as_ptr(),\n215\t        self.d_unstacked_cols.as_ptr(),\n216\t        self.d_lambda_pows.as_ptr(),\n217\t        &mut self.d_accum,\n218\t        stacked_height,\n219\t        l_skip + round,\n220\t    )?;\n221\t}\n222\t\n223\tif !nondegen_descs.is_empty() {\n224\t    let d_nondegen_descs = nondegen_descs.to_device()?;\n225\t    let d_block_offsets = nondegen_block_offsets.to_device()?;\n226\t    batched_stacked_reduction_sumcheck_mle_round(\n227\t        &d_nondegen_descs,\n228\t        &d_block_offsets,\n229\t        total_nondegen_blocks,\n230\t        &self.d_q_eval_ptrs,\n231\t        &self.eq_r_ns,\n232\t        &self.k_rot_ns.buffer,\n233\t        self.d_unstacked_cols.as_ptr(),\n234\t        self.d_lambda_pows.as_ptr(),\n235\t        &mut self.d_accum,\n236\t        stacked_height,\n237\t    )?;\n238\t}\n239\t```\n240\t\n241\t### Change 7: Add stride computation helper\n242\t\n243\t**File**: `crates/cuda-backend/src/cuda/stacked_reduction.rs`\n244\t\n245\tAdd a Rust function `compute_mle_launch_params(num_y: u32, window_len: u32, sm_count: u32) -> (u32, u32)` that replicates the existing auto-tuning heuristic from `stacked_reduction.cu` lines 505-524. This returns `(blocks_x, stride)` for use in descriptor building.\n246\t\n247\tThis keeps the auto-tuning logic accessible from Rust without an FFI call, needed because we build descriptors on the CPU before any kernel launch.\n248\t\n249\t### Change 8: Pre-allocate descriptor buffers (optional optimization)\n250\t\n251\t**File**: `crates/cuda-backend/src/stacked_reduction.rs`\n252\t\n253\tAdd fields to `StackedReductionGpu`:\n254\t```rust\n255\td_degen_descs: DeviceBuffer<DegenMleDesc>,\n256\td_nondegen_descs: DeviceBuffer<NonDegenMleDesc>,\n257\td_block_offsets: DeviceBuffer<u32>,\n258\t```\n259\t\n260\tPre-allocate these with capacity equal to `ht_diff_idxs.len() - 1` during construction. Use `copy_to()` instead of `to_device()` per round to avoid per-round allocation.\n261\t\n262\tThis eliminates ~34 per-round DeviceBuffer allocations (17 rounds × 2 descriptor types). This is a secondary optimization; correctness and the main speedup come from the batched kernels themselves.\n263\t\n264\t## Invariants\n265\t\n266\t1. **Correctness**: The batched kernels must produce identical atomic accumulations to the per-AIR kernels. All kernel arguments and data access patterns must match exactly. The only difference is how blocks are mapped to AIRs.\n267\t\n268\t2. **Atomic accumulator semantics**: All blocks across both batched kernels atomically add to the same `d_accum` buffer. The u64 overflow guarantee holds: at APC 300, total atomic adds = ~608 degenerate blocks + ~2000 non-degenerate blocks = ~2608 adds per accumulator entry, well below the 2^33 overflow limit.\n269\t\n270\t3. **APC 0 path unchanged**: With <100 AIR instances at APC 0, most windows are non-degenerate with large num_y. The batched kernels still handle this correctly — the non-degenerate batch will have fewer descriptors but each with more blocks, and the degenerate batch may be empty.\n271\t\n272\t4. **Descriptor layout matches**: `#[repr(C)]` on Rust structs ensures memory layout matches the CUDA structs. Field order and types must be identical.\n273\t\n274\t5. **Block-to-AIR mapping**: The prefix-sum array for non-degenerate batching must be computed correctly. Each entry `block_prefix_sums[i]` = sum of blocks for descriptors 0..i (exclusive prefix sum). A block with `blockIdx.x == block_prefix_sums[i]` belongs to descriptor `i`.\n275\t\n276\t6. **Stride auto-tuning**: The Rust-side stride computation must exactly replicate the CUDA-side heuristic (lines 505-524 of stacked_reduction.cu) to ensure equivalent parallelism and correctness.\n277\t\n278\t7. **fill_zero and to_host ordering**: `fill_zero(d_accum)` must complete before any batched kernel launch. Both batched kernels must complete before `to_host(d_accum)`. This is guaranteed by same-stream ordering (all on the default stream).\n279\t\n280\t## Measurement Plan\n281\t\n282\t### Before implementation\n283\tRun `openvm-riscv/scripts/run_pairing.sh` in the powdr repo. Save metrics as `before_apc{000,100,300}.json`.\n284\t\n285\t### After implementation\n286\tRun the same benchmark. Save metrics as `after_apc{000,100,300}.json`.\n287\t\n288\t### Verification\n289\t1. All three APC configs must prove + verify successfully (the benchmark script includes verification)\n290\t2. Use `spec.py` to compare before/after metrics\n291\t3. Key metrics to check:\n292\t   - MLE Rounds at APC 300: expect 80-130ms (down from ~182ms)\n293\t   - STARK excl trace at APC 300: expect ~1390-1440ms (down from ~1493ms)\n294\t   - APC 0 STARK excl trace: must not regress >5% (i.e., stay under 2260ms)\n295\t\n296\t### Profiling\n297\tRun nsys on APC 300 after implementation. Verify:\n298\t- Degenerate kernel launches reduced from ~10K to ~17 per benchmark\n299\t- Non-degenerate kernel launches reduced from ~5K to ~17 per benchmark\n300\t- GPU utilization during MLE phase improved\n301\t\n302\t## Rollback Criteria\n303\t\n304\tRevert if ANY of the following:\n305\t1. **MLE Rounds at APC 300 does not improve by at least 30ms** (less than ~17% improvement)\n306\t2. **STARK excl trace at APC 0 regresses by more than 65ms** (>3% regression)\n307\t3. **GPU OOM** on any APC config\n308\t4. **Correctness failure**: prove+verify fails on any APC config\n309\t5. **STARK excl trace at APC 300 does not improve by at least 25ms** (less than ~1.7% overall improvement)\n310\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"8112afd3-6b71-4b0c-b23a-9001717999d3","uuid":"b5d63d50-13a2-4f3f-ba1d-fdff50d15bc3","timestamp":"2026-04-13T04:43:51.625Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/home/georg/stark-backend/autoopt-results/2026-04-13-2300-batch-mle-round-kernels/plan.md","content":"# Plan: Batch MLE Round Kernels\n\n## Goal\n\nReplace the per-AIR kernel launch loop in `batch_sumcheck_poly_eval()` with batched kernel launches using descriptor arrays. This eliminates ~15K individual kernel launches per benchmark at APC 300, improving GPU utilization and reducing host-side overhead.\n\n**Target**: Reduce MLE Rounds from 182ms to ~80-130ms at APC 300 (save 50-100ms). No regression at APC 0.\n\n## Current Code Path\n\n### Rust entry point\n`crates/cuda-backend/src/stacked_reduction.rs:789` — `batch_sumcheck_poly_eval()`\n\nPer MLE round (rounds 1..=n_stack):\n1. **Line 831**: `fill_zero(d_accum)` — zeros the 8-element u64 atomic accumulator\n2. **Line 828**: `eq_ub_per_trace.copy_to(d_eq_ub_all)` — bulk H2D upload (once per round)\n3. **Lines 835-888**: Loop over `ht_diff_idxs.windows(2)`:\n   - Compute per-window pointers: `unstacked_cols_ptr = d_unstacked_cols.as_ptr().add(window[0])`, `lambda_pows_ptr = d_lambda_pows.as_ptr().add(2 * window[0])`\n   - **Line 845**: Branch on `log_height < l_skip + round` → degenerate vs non-degenerate\n   - **Degenerate (line 852)**: `stacked_reduction_sumcheck_mle_round_degenerate()` — 1 block, min(window_len, 256) threads\n   - **Non-degenerate (line 873)**: `stacked_reduction_sumcheck_mle_round()` — grid.x × grid.y blocks with auto-tuned stride\n4. **Line 891**: `d_accum.to_host()` — single D2H copy + CPU reduction\n\n### CUDA kernels\n`crates/cuda-backend/cuda/src/stacked_reduction.cu`\n\n**Degenerate kernel** (line 306): Single block per AIR. Each thread iterates over window columns at stride=blockDim.x. Loads per-column q_eval from global memory, multiplies by eq/lambda factors, accumulates via `block_reduce_sum` + `atomic_add_fpext_to_u64` to shared output.\n\n**Non-degenerate kernel** (line 228): 2D grid (y_dim blocks × window_stride blocks). Each thread handles one y-point, iterates over window columns at stride=gridDim.y. Same atomic accumulation to shared output.\n\nBoth kernels accumulate into the SAME `d_accum` buffer via atomics → all per-AIR launches within a round are data-independent and can execute concurrently.\n\n### FFI bindings\n`crates/cuda-backend/src/cuda/stacked_reduction.rs`\n- Lines 53-64: `_stacked_reduction_sumcheck_mle_round` extern declaration\n- Lines 66-78: `_stacked_reduction_sumcheck_mle_round_degenerate` extern declaration\n- Lines 209-231: Safe wrapper `stacked_reduction_sumcheck_mle_round()`\n- Lines 245-275: Safe wrapper `stacked_reduction_sumcheck_mle_round_degenerate()`\n\n### Why it's slow\n\nAt APC 300 with 2 segments (~311 AIRs/segment, ~17 MLE rounds):\n- **10,348 degenerate kernel launches**: avg 3.9μs each, 40ms total GPU time\n- **5,076 non-degenerate kernel launches**: avg 4.3μs each, 22ms total GPU time\n- **Total**: 15,424 launches, 62ms GPU time, **182ms wall time**\n- **120ms overhead** (66%) from: kernel launch latency (~30ms), GPU pipeline gaps between tiny launches (~40ms), CPU loop overhead (~20ms), sequential execution on single stream preventing SM utilization (~30ms)\n\nEach degenerate launch uses 1 block on 1 SM. The RTX 4090 has 128 SMs. Effective utilization: ~0.8% per launch.\n\n## Changes\n\n### Change 1: Add descriptor structs (CUDA side)\n\n**File**: `crates/cuda-backend/cuda/src/stacked_reduction.cu`\n\nAdd two new structs after the existing `UnstackedSlice` (line 34):\n\n```c\nstruct DegenMleDesc {\n    uint32_t col_offset;    // = window[0], indexes into unstacked_cols, eq_ub, lambda_pows\n    uint32_t window_len;    // = window[1] - window[0]\n    FpExt eq_r;             // from eq_stable[log_height]\n    FpExt k_rot_r;          // from k_rot_stable[log_height]\n};\n\nstruct NonDegenMleDesc {\n    uint32_t col_offset;    // = window[0]\n    uint32_t window_len;    // = window[1] - window[0]\n    uint32_t num_y;         // = 1 << (log_height - l_skip - round)\n    uint32_t stride;        // auto-tuned grid.y from existing heuristic\n    uint32_t blocks_x;      // = ceil(num_y / 256)\n};\n```\n\n### Change 2: Add batched degenerate kernel (CUDA side)\n\n**File**: `crates/cuda-backend/cuda/src/stacked_reduction.cu`\n\nAdd new kernel after the existing degenerate kernel (after line 368):\n\n```cuda\n__global__ void batched_degenerate_mle_round_kernel(\n    const DegenMleDesc *__restrict__ descs,\n    const FpExt *__restrict__ const *__restrict__ q_evals,\n    const FpExt *__restrict__ eq_ub_base,\n    const UnstackedSlice *__restrict__ unstacked_cols_base,\n    const FpExt *__restrict__ lambda_pows_base,\n    uint64_t *__restrict__ output,\n    uint32_t q_height,\n    uint32_t shift_factor)\n```\n\n**Grid**: `(num_degenerate_airs, 1)`, **Block**: `(256, 1)`\n\nEach block reads `descs[blockIdx.x]` to get its col_offset, window_len, eq_r, k_rot_r. Computes base pointers: `eq_ub_ptr = eq_ub_base + desc.col_offset`, `unstacked_cols = unstacked_cols_base + desc.col_offset`, `lambda_pows = lambda_pows_base + 2 * desc.col_offset`. Body is identical to existing degenerate kernel (lines 328-358) but using descriptor fields instead of kernel args. Threads with `threadIdx.x >= desc.window_len` contribute zero to the reduction (handled naturally by the for-loop bounds).\n\n### Change 3: Add batched non-degenerate kernel (CUDA side)\n\n**File**: `crates/cuda-backend/cuda/src/stacked_reduction.cu`\n\nAdd new kernel after the batched degenerate kernel:\n\n```cuda\n__global__ void batched_nondegen_mle_round_kernel(\n    const NonDegenMleDesc *__restrict__ descs,\n    const uint32_t *__restrict__ block_prefix_sums,\n    uint32_t num_descs,\n    const FpExt *__restrict__ const *__restrict__ q_evals,\n    const FpExt *__restrict__ eq_r_ns,\n    const FpExt *__restrict__ k_rot_ns,\n    const UnstackedSlice *__restrict__ unstacked_cols_base,\n    const FpExt *__restrict__ lambda_pows_base,\n    uint64_t *__restrict__ output,\n    uint32_t q_height)\n```\n\n**Grid**: `(total_blocks, 1)` where `total_blocks = sum of (blocks_x * stride) for all non-degenerate AIRs`, **Block**: `(256, 1)`\n\nEach block uses binary search on `block_prefix_sums` to find its AIR index (`air_idx`), then computes its local block index within that AIR. Decomposes local index into `(local_x, local_y) = (local_block % blocks_x, local_block / blocks_x)`. Maps to `y_int = local_x * 256 + threadIdx.x` and `window_idx_base = local_y`. Rest of computation is identical to existing non-degenerate kernel (lines 254-291).\n\nBinary search is O(log N) per block — at most ~10 comparisons for 600 AIRs. Negligible overhead.\n\n### Change 4: Add launcher functions (CUDA side)\n\n**File**: `crates/cuda-backend/cuda/src/stacked_reduction.cu`\n\nAdd two new extern \"C\" launcher functions after the existing launchers (after line 570):\n\n`_batched_stacked_reduction_sumcheck_mle_round_degenerate`:\n- Receives: descs ptr, num_descs, shared array pointers, q_height, shift_factor\n- Grid: `(num_descs, 1)`, Block: `(256, 1)`\n- shmem: `div_ceil(256, WARP_SIZE) * sizeof(FpExt) = 8 * 16 = 128 bytes`\n\n`_batched_stacked_reduction_sumcheck_mle_round`:\n- Receives: descs ptr, block_prefix_sums ptr, num_descs, total_blocks, shared array pointers, q_height\n- Grid: `(total_blocks, 1)`, Block: `(256, 1)`\n- shmem: same 128 bytes\n- Computes auto-tuned stride per descriptor using existing heuristic (lines 505-524), populates stride and blocks_x fields on the host side (Rust) before upload.\n\n### Change 5: Add Rust descriptor types and FFI bindings\n\n**File**: `crates/cuda-backend/src/cuda/stacked_reduction.rs`\n\nAdd `#[repr(C)]` Rust structs matching the CUDA descriptors:\n\n```rust\n#[repr(C)]\n#[derive(Clone, Copy)]\npub(crate) struct DegenMleDesc {\n    col_offset: u32,\n    window_len: u32,\n    eq_r: EF,\n    k_rot_r: EF,\n}\n\n#[repr(C)]\n#[derive(Clone, Copy)]\npub(crate) struct NonDegenMleDesc {\n    col_offset: u32,\n    window_len: u32,\n    num_y: u32,\n    stride: u32,\n    blocks_x: u32,\n}\n```\n\nAdd extern declarations for the new launcher functions. Add safe Rust wrappers that take `&DeviceBuffer<DegenMleDesc>` / `&DeviceBuffer<NonDegenMleDesc>` and the shared base pointers.\n\n### Change 6: Modify batch_sumcheck_poly_eval to use batched launches\n\n**File**: `crates/cuda-backend/src/stacked_reduction.rs`\n\nReplace the per-window loop (lines 835-888) with:\n\n**Phase A — Build descriptors** (CPU-only, no CUDA calls):\n```rust\nlet mut degen_descs: Vec<DegenMleDesc> = Vec::new();\nlet mut nondegen_descs: Vec<NonDegenMleDesc> = Vec::new();\nlet mut nondegen_block_offsets: Vec<u32> = Vec::new();\nlet mut total_nondegen_blocks: u32 = 0;\n\nfor window in self.ht_diff_idxs.windows(2) {\n    let col_offset = window[0] as u32;\n    let window_len = (window[1] - window[0]) as u32;\n    let log_height = self.unstacked_cols[window[0]].log_height as usize;\n\n    if log_height < l_skip + round {\n        degen_descs.push(DegenMleDesc {\n            col_offset,\n            window_len,\n            eq_r: self.eq_stable[log_height],\n            k_rot_r: self.k_rot_stable[log_height],\n        });\n    } else {\n        let hypercube_dim = log_height - l_skip - round;\n        let num_y = 1u32 << hypercube_dim;\n        let (blocks_x, stride) = compute_mle_launch_params(num_y, window_len, self.sm_count);\n        nondegen_block_offsets.push(total_nondegen_blocks);\n        total_nondegen_blocks += blocks_x * stride;\n        nondegen_descs.push(NonDegenMleDesc {\n            col_offset, window_len, num_y, stride, blocks_x,\n        });\n    }\n}\n```\n\n**Phase B — Upload descriptors and launch batched kernels**:\n```rust\nif !degen_descs.is_empty() {\n    let d_degen_descs = degen_descs.to_device()?;\n    batched_stacked_reduction_sumcheck_mle_round_degenerate(\n        &d_degen_descs,\n        &self.d_q_eval_ptrs,\n        self.d_eq_ub_all.as_ptr(),\n        self.d_unstacked_cols.as_ptr(),\n        self.d_lambda_pows.as_ptr(),\n        &mut self.d_accum,\n        stacked_height,\n        l_skip + round,\n    )?;\n}\n\nif !nondegen_descs.is_empty() {\n    let d_nondegen_descs = nondegen_descs.to_device()?;\n    let d_block_offsets = nondegen_block_offsets.to_device()?;\n    batched_stacked_reduction_sumcheck_mle_round(\n        &d_nondegen_descs,\n        &d_block_offsets,\n        total_nondegen_blocks,\n        &self.d_q_eval_ptrs,\n        &self.eq_r_ns,\n        &self.k_rot_ns.buffer,\n        self.d_unstacked_cols.as_ptr(),\n        self.d_lambda_pows.as_ptr(),\n        &mut self.d_accum,\n        stacked_height,\n    )?;\n}\n```\n\n### Change 7: Add stride computation helper\n\n**File**: `crates/cuda-backend/src/cuda/stacked_reduction.rs`\n\nAdd a Rust function `compute_mle_launch_params(num_y: u32, window_len: u32, sm_count: u32) -> (u32, u32)` that replicates the existing auto-tuning heuristic from `stacked_reduction.cu` lines 505-524. This returns `(blocks_x, stride)` for use in descriptor building.\n\nThis keeps the auto-tuning logic accessible from Rust without an FFI call, needed because we build descriptors on the CPU before any kernel launch.\n\n### Change 8: Pre-allocate descriptor buffers (optional optimization)\n\n**File**: `crates/cuda-backend/src/stacked_reduction.rs`\n\nAdd fields to `StackedReductionGpu`:\n```rust\nd_degen_descs: DeviceBuffer<DegenMleDesc>,\nd_nondegen_descs: DeviceBuffer<NonDegenMleDesc>,\nd_block_offsets: DeviceBuffer<u32>,\n```\n\nPre-allocate these with capacity equal to `ht_diff_idxs.len() - 1` during construction. Use `copy_to()` instead of `to_device()` per round to avoid per-round allocation.\n\nThis eliminates ~34 per-round DeviceBuffer allocations (17 rounds × 2 descriptor types). This is a secondary optimization; correctness and the main speedup come from the batched kernels themselves.\n\n## Invariants\n\n1. **Correctness**: The batched kernels must produce identical atomic accumulations to the per-AIR kernels. All kernel arguments and data access patterns must match exactly. The only difference is how blocks are mapped to AIRs.\n\n2. **Atomic accumulator semantics**: All blocks across both batched kernels atomically add to the same `d_accum` buffer. The u64 overflow guarantee holds: at APC 300, total atomic adds = ~608 degenerate blocks + ~2000 non-degenerate blocks = ~2608 adds per accumulator entry, well below the 2^33 overflow limit.\n\n3. **APC 0 path unchanged**: With <100 AIR instances at APC 0, most windows are non-degenerate with large num_y. The batched kernels still handle this correctly — the non-degenerate batch will have fewer descriptors but each with more blocks, and the degenerate batch may be empty.\n\n4. **Descriptor layout matches**: `#[repr(C)]` on Rust structs ensures memory layout matches the CUDA structs. Field order and types must be identical.\n\n5. **Block-to-AIR mapping**: The prefix-sum array for non-degenerate batching must be computed correctly. Each entry `block_prefix_sums[i]` = sum of blocks for descriptors 0..i (exclusive prefix sum). A block with `blockIdx.x == block_prefix_sums[i]` belongs to descriptor `i`.\n\n6. **Stride auto-tuning**: The Rust-side stride computation must exactly replicate the CUDA-side heuristic (lines 505-524 of stacked_reduction.cu) to ensure equivalent parallelism and correctness.\n\n7. **fill_zero and to_host ordering**: `fill_zero(d_accum)` must complete before any batched kernel launch. Both batched kernels must complete before `to_host(d_accum)`. This is guaranteed by same-stream ordering (all on the default stream).\n\n## Measurement Plan\n\n### Before implementation\nRun `openvm-riscv/scripts/run_pairing.sh` in the powdr repo. Save metrics as `before_apc{000,100,300}.json`.\n\n### After implementation\nRun the same benchmark. Save metrics as `after_apc{000,100,300}.json`.\n\n### Verification\n1. All three APC configs must prove + verify successfully (the benchmark script includes verification)\n2. Use `spec.py` to compare before/after metrics\n3. Key metrics to check:\n   - MLE Rounds at APC 300: expect 80-130ms (down from ~182ms)\n   - STARK excl trace at APC 300: expect ~1390-1440ms (down from ~1493ms)\n   - APC 0 STARK excl trace: must not regress >5% (i.e., stay under 2260ms)\n\n### Profiling\nRun nsys on APC 300 after implementation. Verify:\n- Degenerate kernel launches reduced from ~10K to ~17 per benchmark\n- Non-degenerate kernel launches reduced from ~5K to ~17 per benchmark\n- GPU utilization during MLE phase improved\n\n## Rollback Criteria\n\nRevert if ANY of the following:\n1. **MLE Rounds at APC 300 does not improve by at least 30ms** (less than ~17% improvement)\n2. **STARK excl trace at APC 0 regresses by more than 65ms** (>3% regression)\n3. **GPU OOM** on any APC config\n4. **Correctness failure**: prove+verify fails on any APC config\n5. **STARK excl trace at APC 300 does not improve by at least 25ms** (less than ~1.7% overall improvement)\n","numLines":310,"startLine":1,"totalLines":310}}}
